{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A lab analyst observes a sample of a substance. An exponential model estimates that the mass, in grams, of the sample decreases by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"24 percent sign\"><mn>24</mn><mo>%</mo></math> every <math alttext=\"22.96\"><mn>22.96</mn>\n</math> minutes. Which of the following equations could represent this model, where <math alttext=\"upper M\"><mi>M</mi>\n</math> is the estimated mass, in grams, of the sample <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> minutes after the lab analyst began observing the sample?</p>", "keys": ["eff1b5a2-8929-42b9-8fe1-bc1ca8c29b4b"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "fec1af7f-c89a-4f34-9dec-be10c7ee3fc4", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"upper M equals 100 left parenthesis 0.24 right parenthesis Superscript t plus 22.96\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.24</mn></mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>22.96</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"}, {"id": "5bbb40d8-e85c-4c3d-94c9-36db646e20a1", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"upper M equals 100 left parenthesis 0.24 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 22.96 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.24</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>22.96</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"}, {"id": "5f9ecca3-5063-466f-94df-8d32856fe0e8", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"upper M equals 100 left parenthesis 0.76 right parenthesis Superscript t plus 22.96\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.76</mn></mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>22.96</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"}, {"id": "eff1b5a2-8929-42b9-8fe1-bc1ca8c29b4b", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"upper M equals 100 left parenthesis 0.76 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 22.96 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.76</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>22.96</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p>Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the mass of a sample of a substance decreases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"24 percent sign\"><mn>24</mn><mo>%</mo></math> every&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22.96\"><mn>22.96</mn></math> minutes. Therefore, after each <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22.96\"><mn>22.96</mn></math>-minute interval the mass is multiplied by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1 minus 0.24\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>0.24</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0.76\"><mn>0.76</mn></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> represents the number of minutes after the lab analyst began observing the sample; therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction t Over 22.96 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>22.96</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;represents the number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22.96\"><mn>22.96</mn></math>-minute intervals. The equation that could represent this model is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper M equals 100 left parenthesis 0.76 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction t Over 22.96 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0.76</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>22.96</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper M\"><mi>M</mi></math> is the estimated mass, in grams, of the sample&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> minutes after the lab analyst began observing it.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "397302ed-5a13-4b95-9bee-c626b3a9e221", "correct_answer": ["D"]}